# Read by Vite at build time, and by `vitepress dev` too, so the site behaves the same in both.
#
# VitePress's router intercepts a click on any same-origin link whose file extension it does not
# recognise and answers it in-app, as a page. Its list of recognised extensions has `xml` on it
# and not `rss` -- so every link to /blog/feed.rss on this site (the footer, the home page, the
# blog index, the about page) was swallowed by the router and answered with a 404, while the
# file itself sat there being served correctly to anyone who typed the URL.
#
# This is the documented way to add to that list. `.vitepress/feed.mjs` checks it took effect,
# because the failure is silent: the feed still builds, the links still point at it, and only a
# click finds out.
VITE_EXTRA_EXTENSIONS=rss
